{"description":"High-frequency SAT words every test-taker should know.","module":"Vocabulary Essentials","questions":[{"answer":0,"explain":"Abate = to subside or lessen (e.g., 'the storm abated').","options":["to lessen in intensity","to abandon completely","to praise highly","to build up"],"q":"ABATE most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Benevolent = well-meaning, kindly (bene = good).","options":["kind and generous","strict and severe","wealthy and powerful","shy and reserved"],"q":"BENEVOLENT most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Candid = truthful and straightforward, even when uncomfortable.","options":["frank and honest","hidden and secret","polite but false","confused and lost"],"q":"CANDID most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Ephemeral = fleeting, short-lived (e.g., fame, trends).","options":["lasting a very short time","eternal and unchanging","extremely large","barely visible"],"q":"EPHEMERAL most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Fortuitous = lucky accident. (Not the same as fortunate, but close.)","options":["happening by lucky chance","carefully planned","extremely unfortunate","deliberately harmful"],"q":"FORTUITOUS most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Hackneyed = clichéd, worn out from overuse.","options":["overused and unoriginal","deeply meaningful","brand new","cleverly hidden"],"q":"HACKNEYED most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Immutable = not capable of change (in- = not, mut = change).","options":["unchangeable","immoral","invisible","impatient"],"q":"IMMUTABLE most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Laconic = brief, economical with words.","options":["using few words","talkative and loud","confusing and vague","angry and bitter"],"q":"LACONIC most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Meticulous = showing great attention to detail.","options":["extremely careful and precise","messy and careless","quick and sloppy","creative but disorganized"],"q":"METICULOUS most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Nonchalant = relaxed, casually calm.","options":["calm and unconcerned","extremely nervous","deeply passionate","openly hostile"],"q":"NONCHALANT most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Obfuscate = to muddy, make unclear (ob- = against, fusc = dark).","options":["to deliberately confuse or obscure","to clarify completely","to obey promptly","to observe quietly"],"q":"OBFUSCATE most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Pragmatic = dealing with problems practically.","options":["practical rather than idealistic","theoretical and abstract","stubborn and rigid","playful and carefree"],"q":"PRAGMATIC most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Reticent = holding back in speech, reserved.","options":["reserved; reluctant to speak","eager to talk","rude and abrupt","honest to a fault"],"q":"RETICENT most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Scrutinize = to inspect with great care.","options":["to examine closely","to glance quickly","to ignore deliberately","to praise publicly"],"q":"SCRUTINIZE most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Juxtapose = side-by-side placement to highlight differences.","options":["to place side by side for contrast","to separate permanently","to judge harshly","to join into one"],"q":"JUXTAPOSE most nearly means…"},{"answer":0,"explain":"Deference = yielding out of respect (e.g., 'in deference to her experience').","options":["respectful submission to another's judgment","complete indifference","open rebellion","careless disregard"],"q":"DEFERENCE most nearly means…"}],"rounds":[{"boss":false,"count":16,"desc":"16 high-frequency SAT words. Nail the definitions.","tag":"Module 1","title":"Vocabulary Essentials"}],"subject":"SAT Prep","title":"SAT Vocabulary Essentials"}